      "id": 1,
      "text": "Aiken, Texas was named after Herman Aiken, a local pioneer who helped establish the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/aiken-tx-shelby-county",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Aiken’s first post office opened in 1889 and was called a “country post office” in an 1890 report.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/aiken-tx-shelby-county",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1892 Aiken boasted a sawmill, a blacksmith’s shop, and a school, serving the surrounding farms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/aiken-tx-shelby-county",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The post office closed in 1909, but the town kept its church and school as community hubs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/aiken-tx-shelby-county",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Aiken’s school continued to educate local children long after the post office shut down.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/aiken-tx-shelby-county",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Today, Aiken remains a small, close‑knit community centered around its historic church and school.",
